// NOTE: this line used to be
//     assert(cave+3FF0,4c 45 50 52 41 43 33 3a 46 49 58 45 44 3a 31 00)
// i.e. the "LEPRAC3:FIXED:1" version marker the ORIGINAL practice mod kept at
// cave+0x3FF0.  cea's assert() does not only CHECK -- it WRITES the byte list
// into the image.  Our own data section has since grown over that range, so
// the write was silently stamping those 15 bytes across
// OVL_STAGE / OVL_TXTCNT / SEED_USED / OVL_PREV_SEEDSW / OVL_TYPE_ON, turning
// OVL_STAGE into 0x4C000000 ("...\0\0\0L") -- and ovl_mirror dereferenced it
// on the very first frame.  That was the crash.  The marker is preserved as
// ordinary labelled data at the END of our block instead; see LEPRAC_MARK.
